[model call 2026-10-11T12:56:42Z] claude-opus-5-5 (Claude Agent SDK) self-test fix turn 27: text
I made one small edit to the router prompt in `out/main-rB.workflow.json`, and the file loads with python3. This test run wasn't a fair test, though. The record shows the platform failed partway through with `402 Insufficient credits`. In the failed calls the agent asked for verification again *after* the account had been disclosed, and the tools ran a second time (`verify_identity` … `get_account`). That looks like the session restarting rather than anything the workflow tells it to do. The router node has no path back to identity, and the "technical issue, please use the mobile app" message isn't in the workflow, so it most likely came from the platform. All three checks are things the brief really requires for these customers. They need a rerun once credits are topped up before we can trust the results.

The one real problem I could see: twice, in the node that handles the customer's first answer, the agent spoke when it should have handed over to the right next step. It did its own read-back ("Just to confirm… Is that correct?") instead of moving to the negotiation step. And it said "I am sorry for your loss… One moment please" instead of moving to the hardship step. I added a general rule to that node: after stating the debts, it must never read back, confirm or record a promise, never say sympathy or "one moment", and must only move the call on to the next step. Nothing else changed.

- **Daniel, "create_promise must be called"**: partly fixed. The router no longer does its own read-back, so the yes now leads to the proper read-back and `create_promise`. The failure itself was mainly the platform error ("technical issue") straight after his yes.
- **Marcus, `add_note` paid / dispute / refused**: not fixed by any edit. The paid, dispute and refused paths and their note rules are already in the workflow (Brief B clauses 8–9). The call never got there because the session restarted (the identity check repeated after the debts were stated), which points to the credits error.
- **Lena, `transfer_to_agent` support and close `support` instead of `human`**: partly fixed. The new router rule stops the agent replying itself to the job loss, so it should go straight to the hardship step, which offers the support transfer. The session restart also hit this call, and the close as `human` happened during that broken stretch.

